is at risk of collapsing  the unstable roof seems ready to cave in  but she  her two children and five grandchildren  have nowhere else to go  for now they've been given monetary  assistance  we're very happy we've had help with  groceries i get 150 dollars a month to  shop  but the main reason she's happy is that  the albanian government  is giving her family an apartment in  these new developments in sumana  about 30 kilometers north of the capital  tirana  five buildings collapsed here when a  powerful earthquake struck albania in  2019  killing two dozen people in sumana alone  but anyone who lost their house will  receive a new one for free  and the government is paying their rent  in the meantime part of a dynamic  response to turn adversity to advantage  in the port of duras there are few signs  left that 25 people were killed by  collapsing hotels and houses  the sites of tragedy have been bulldozed  clean and listing buildings removed  we succeeded to transform the  response to the earthquake in a  success story people supported us  mostly because of how we reacted  exactly to covet an earthquake  so we turned these two blows  in two opportunities to  prove that we can we can do  we can do great things together and we  did the government has spent 150 million  dollars on earthquake reconstruction  this year alone  but the timing has been political more  than half that aid  was dispersed during the month before  april's general election  that helped prime minister eddie rama  win a third term  but it also means that for many people  their compensation arrived 18 months  after the earthquake  prolonging their misery ramazan dachi's  family say they haven't received  anything yet  municipal engineers didn't tell him his  damaged home is safe  guaranteed we sleep in fear that there  could be another earthquake and we'll  suffer more damage we have no assurance  that we're safe we're staying at our own  risk and we're very afraid  we've even disabled the front door lock  so we can run out into the street at a  moment's  local authorities gave dachi this tent  but he never used it  his neighbors told us they spent a year  in their tent and  ended up fixing their house at their own  expense  at the heart of this community 70 units  are going up first  to house the last of those still  homeless it's unclear whether people  will get to keep their damaged  properties  but eddie rama's earthquake response was  first and it helped him win an election  john saropolos al-jazeera thumana  albania
 

